  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/EggyStudio/BevyCSharp",
  "published": "2026-11-14T17:22:52.897Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Blockout's play reads the recipe where the game says it saved it and puts that file back as it was, since a game built in Debug saves into its project's assets folder, which the guide says.\nA game run under dotnet watch has its changed behaviors registered again at the next frame, a system named again kept where it stands and one whose method a change took out passed over at its throw, with the guide saying which edits wait for the next start, BUILDING.md naming the release that keeps the bridge's symbols and AGENTS.md naming what each profile adds.\nThe ambient's kernel sums every workgroup of a probe's rays where each texel sends four, so the indirect light of a panel too wide to be carried as a glow light goes within two frames of the panel going dark, as a new test of a room lit by such a panel reads.\nThe bridge builds each asset source's watcher itself, warning of a folder the system will not watch and reading it unwatched and resolving a root reached through a link, a Debug game reads and watches its project's assets folder with its shader cache under obj, a script build that throws or cannot read a file leaves nothing of itself running, the app decides watching once for its whole run, and the workflow runs the renderer's tests on every system.\nA scene loaded at the top level is spawned again in place when its file's bytes change, keeping the program's own entities and leaving an open document to a tool that keeps it, every file read again is posted as AssetReloaded and listed in live.status, ./bcs open leaves watching out with --no-watch, and the guide says the live path.\nBehavior scripts compile through a ScriptsPlugin that the editor, the Player and a game referencing the project add, which builds them again when one is saved while the app watches its assets, says each build in the log and answers scripts.reload and scripts.status.\nThe render profile's bridges carry Bevy's asset watcher, which watches where the config asks and a program's Debug build asks by default, and a file read again is said as AssetReloaded and a scene spawned again in place as a reload.",
